#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:268
msgid "Confidence Threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:274
msgid ""
"Confidence Threshold\n"
"\n"
"Minimum probability (0.0 to 1.0) for a detection to count as valid.\n"
"• Raise it (e.g. 0.50) if there are many 'false positives' "
"(noise/ghosts).\n"
"• Lower it (e.g. 0.15) if the fish is not detected in some frames.\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.25"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:285
msgid "NMS Threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:291
msgid ""
"NMS Threshold (Non-Maximum Suppression)\n"
"\n"
"Controls the removal of duplicate boxes for the same object.\n"
"• Low values (e.g. 0.4) merge overlapping boxes aggressively.\n"
"• High values (e.g. 0.7) allow more overlap.\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.50"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:306
msgid "Use ByteTrack (Advanced Tracking)"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:335
msgid "Track Thresh:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:341
msgid ""
"Track Threshold (Tracking)\n"
"\n"
"Minimum confidence to START or KEEP a track.\n"
"• Defines how 'sure' the detector must be to create a new ID.\n"
"• Raise it to avoid junk/noise tracks.\n"
"• Lower it to keep the ID of fish that are hard to detect.\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.25"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:352
msgid "Match Thresh:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:358
msgid ""
"Match Threshold\n"
"\n"
"Tolerance for associating a new detection with an existing track.\n"
"• High values (e.g. 0.8+) are more permissive (good for fast movement).\n"
"• Low values (<0.5) are restrictive (avoids identity swaps, but may lose "
"the track).\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.95"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:370
msgid "Track Buffer:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:376
msgid ""
"Track Buffer (Memory)\n"
"\n"
"How many frames the system 'remembers' a fish after it disappears "
"(occlusion/miss).\n"
"• Raise it (e.g. 120) if the fish vanishes for a long time.\n"
"• Lower it to drop lost tracks quickly.\n"
"• Default: 90 frames (~3s at 30fps)"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:387
msgid "Max Dist. (px):"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:393
msgid ""
"Maximum Distance (pixels)\n"
"\n"
"How far the centre of the fish may move between processed frames.\n"
"• Prevents impossible associations (teleporting).\n"
"• Raise it if the fish is fast or the frame rate is low.\n"
"• Lower it if IDs are swapped between distant fish.\n"
"• Default: 400.0 px"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:405
msgid "IoU Thresh:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:411
msgid ""
"IoU Threshold (Tracking)\n"
"\n"
"Minimum overlap (Intersection over Union) to associate boxes.\n"
"• Default: 0.05 (undemanding).\n"
"• Raise it (e.g. 0.3) to require the fish to stay in almost the same "
"position.\n"
"• Lower it to allow abrupt movements that change the box area."
msgstr ""

